module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.TwistCohomologyMonomial
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.BinaryFormBasis

/-!
# The monomial basis of the sections of a twist on the projective line

Let `R` be a commutative ring and `d ≥ 0`.  The degree-`d` homogeneous polynomials in two
variables are free of rank `d + 1` on the monomials `T₀^{d-j} T₁^j`, which is
`MvPolynomial.homogeneousBinaryBasis`.  The degree-zero row of [Stacks, Tag 01XT],
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.twistCohomologyIsoHomogeneous`, identifies that module with
`H⁰(𝐏¹_R, 𝒪(d))`; and sections over an open are left exact, so their zeroth right derived
functor is themselves and `H⁰(𝐏¹_R, 𝒪(d))` is the honest module of global sections
`Γ(𝐏¹_R, 𝒪(d))`.  Transporting the basis along the two identifications makes `Γ(𝐏¹_R, 𝒪(d))`
free of rank `d + 1` over `R`.

This is the input the Stacks proof of [Stacks, Tag 0C2K] needs from the geometry of the
projective line: a section of `𝒪(d)` on `𝐏¹_k` is a degree-`d` form in two coordinates, in
exactly one way.  The spanning half is what makes the `n`-th step of the filtration of the
formal neighbourhood of an exceptional curve generated by the degree-`n` monomials modulo the
`(n+1)`-st step, and the independence half is the linear independence of those monomials over
the residue field.

The degree-zero case of the second identification is
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.twistCohomologyZeroIsoGlobalSections`, which goes on to pass
from `𝒪(0)` to the structure sheaf; without that last step the same construction works in every
degree.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.twistCohomologyZeroIsoSections` — `H⁰(ℙⁿ_R, 𝒪(d))` is the
  module of global sections of `𝒪(d)`, for every `d`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.projectiveLineTwistSectionsBasis` — **`Γ(𝐏¹_R, 𝒪(d))` is
  free of rank `d + 1`** for `d ≥ 0`, on the monomial basis transported along Tag 01XT.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C2K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C2K)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory MvPolynomial
open Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology

universe u

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

namespace Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R]

/-- **`H⁰(ℙⁿ_R, 𝒪(d))` is the module of global sections of `𝒪(d)`**, for every `d`: sections
over an open are left exact, so their zeroth right derived functor is themselves.  This is
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.twistCohomologyZeroIsoGlobalSections` without the passage
from `𝒪(0)` to the structure sheaf, hence available in every degree. -/
def twistCohomologyZeroIsoSections (n : ℕ) (d : ℤ) :
    twistCohomology R n d 0 ≅
      (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} (coeffScalar R n)).obj
        ((Stacks.Cohomology.sectionsFunctor (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R n)) ⊤).obj
          (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf (polyGrading R n) d)) :=
  (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} (coeffScalar R n)).mapIso
    ((Stacks.Cohomology.sectionsFunctor (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R n))
      ⊤).rightDerivedZeroIsoSelf.app _)

/-- **The global sections of `𝒪(d)` on the projective line are free of rank `d + 1`**, for
`d ≥ 0`, on the monomial basis of the degree-`d` binary forms transported along the degree-zero
row of [Stacks, Tag 01XT].  The coefficients act through the structure morphism
`𝐏¹_R ⟶ Spec R`. -/
def projectiveLineTwistSectionsBasis (d : ℤ) (hd : 0 ≤ d) :
    Module.Basis (Fin (d.toNat + 1)) R
      ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} (coeffScalar R 1)).obj
        ((Stacks.Cohomology.sectionsFunctor (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading R 1)) ⊤).obj
          (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf (polyGrading R 1) d))) :=
  (homogeneousBinaryBasis R d.toNat).map
    (((twistCohomologyIsoHomogeneous R 1 d hd).symm ≪≫
      twistCohomologyZeroIsoSections R 1 d).toLinearEquiv)

end Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology
